41	/**
42	 * Helps to traverse (or reduce) a Document (or parts of it) and tracks at the same time the corresponding Schema types.
43	 * <p>
44	 * This is an important distinction to just traversing the Document without any type information: Each field has a clearly
45	 * defined type. See {@link QueryVisitorFieldEnvironment}.
46	 * <p>
47	 * Further are the built in Directives skip/include automatically evaluated: if parts of the Document should be ignored they will not
48	 * be visited. But this is not a full evaluation of a Query: every fragment will be visited/followed regardless of the type condition.
49	 *
50	 * It also doesn't consider field merging, which means for example {@code { user{firstName} user{firstName}} } will result in four
51	 * visitField calls.
52	 */
